1
00:00:45,460 --> 00:00:46,813
I'm so glad to be here.

2
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:03,640
Thank you.

3
00:01:30,040 --> 00:01:34,257
Cody and I destroyed the Control Spire in
Australia with a little help from Santa,

4
00:01:34,340 --> 00:01:36,617
who was actually Hogan,
a friend of Geni's.

5
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,317
We saw a down-under
Digidestined kid named Derek

6
00:01:39,400 --> 00:01:42,282
windsurfing and being
chased by some bad Digimon.

7
00:01:42,460 --> 00:01:44,360
But a Gokimon, Armadimon,

8
00:01:44,520 --> 00:01:47,677
and Crabmon got rid of them before
they became the Blue Flayed Special.

9
00:01:47,760 --> 00:01:51,260
Meanwhile in Paris, TK and
Tai, along with TK's grandpa,

10
00:01:51,680 --> 00:01:55,497
found the Mamemon brothers holding a French
Digidestined girl, Catherine, hostage.

11
00:01:55,580 --> 00:01:58,777
They rescued her, but not before
taking a pie or two in the face.

12
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:00,057
I'm allergic to meringue.

13
00:02:00,140 --> 00:02:00,970
Oh, well.

14
00:02:01,053 --> 00:02:01,883
Viva la France!

15
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,280
Purity! Portiski!

16
00:02:06,660 --> 00:02:07,660
Direct set!

17
00:02:16,140 --> 00:02:17,140
Hey, look!

18
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:18,399
What is this size?

19
00:02:18,800 --> 00:02:21,320
Is it a monster? Is it a monster?

20
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:23,980
There it is!

21
00:02:25,600 --> 00:02:26,800
Howling Blaster!

22
00:02:30,260 --> 00:02:31,142
Spiking strike!

23
00:02:36,640 --> 00:02:38,300
Yeah! Hey, Matt! Huh?

24
00:02:38,400 --> 00:02:41,637
The renegade Digimon are trying to hide
in the Mayan ruins to the east of here.

25
00:02:41,720 --> 00:02:43,997
We better get over there before
they take the place apart.

26
00:02:44,080 --> 00:02:45,340
Good plan. Let's go.

27
00:02:49,420 --> 00:02:51,217
Where are the Mexican Digidestined?

28
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,077
I thought they were supposed to meet us.

29
00:02:53,160 --> 00:02:55,101
They have a curfew for kids here.

30
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:57,754
So it's four of us to how many of them?

31
00:02:58,100 --> 00:02:59,540
I don't like those odds.

32
00:02:59,740 --> 00:03:01,446
Nobody said it would be easy.

33
00:03:02,080 --> 00:03:02,910
That's true.

34
00:03:03,040 --> 00:03:03,877
Don't worry, Matt.

35
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:04,790
We'll even the odds.

36
00:03:04,873 --> 00:03:05,917
That's what I'm afraid of.

37
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:08,737
Wait until those guards get a
good look at you and Wormon.

38
00:03:08,820 --> 00:03:09,650
So they don't.

39
00:03:09,740 --> 00:03:11,328
You and I will go in first.

40
00:03:11,420 --> 00:03:13,117
The Digimon can sneak behind us.

41
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:14,030
Right.

42
00:03:14,840 --> 00:03:15,837
Stop right there!

43
00:03:15,920 --> 00:03:16,750
Please let us by.

44
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:18,077
I think my little sister's in there.

45
00:03:18,160 --> 00:03:19,517
Just how dumb do you think I am?

46
00:03:19,600 --> 00:03:21,857
You little pumps just want to
get in there and tag the ruins.

47
00:03:21,940 --> 00:03:23,980
Tag the ruins? Huh? Huh?

48
00:03:26,840 --> 00:03:27,980
Calm down, guys.

49
00:03:28,160 --> 00:03:30,597
There's no need for an
international incident here.

50
00:03:30,680 --> 00:03:32,137
Okay, that is a little spooky.

51
00:03:32,220 --> 00:03:33,050
Calm down.

52
00:03:33,133 --> 00:03:33,963
He's just kidding.

53
00:03:34,520 --> 00:03:36,157
The direct approach didn't work.

54
00:03:36,240 --> 00:03:37,337
There has to be another way in.

55
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:38,637
We just have to find it.

56
00:03:38,720 --> 00:03:39,550
Exactly.

57
00:03:39,633 --> 00:03:44,031
Oh, but first, Ken, what did that guard
back there say to make you so angry?

58
00:03:44,120 --> 00:03:45,817
There's enough of Ken to go around.

59
00:03:45,900 --> 00:03:47,477
Let's not forget why we're here, okay?

60
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:49,357
There was a time when that
would have been a compliment.

61
00:03:49,440 --> 00:03:50,440
Yeah, I guess so.

62
00:03:50,580 --> 00:03:51,617
Times have changed.

63
00:03:51,700 --> 00:03:52,935
Yeah, for the better.

64
00:03:58,280 --> 00:04:00,520
So much for sneaking in the back door.

65
00:04:00,800 --> 00:04:02,697
They're not taking any chances here.

66
00:04:02,780 --> 00:04:04,817
But it's already crawling with Digimon.

67
00:04:04,900 --> 00:04:05,730
Ironic.

68
00:04:05,813 --> 00:04:07,920
Good thing I'm here, eh? Huh?

69
00:04:09,080 --> 00:04:10,300
Ah, my manners.

70
00:04:10,540 --> 00:04:12,834
I am Jose, Genai's Mexican counterpart.

71
00:04:13,140 --> 00:04:15,097
You sure know how to
make an entrance, Jose.

72
00:04:15,180 --> 00:04:16,010
Great timing, too.

73
00:04:16,093 --> 00:04:17,417
Can you help us get inside?

74
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:18,330
Piece of cake.

75
00:04:18,500 --> 00:04:20,677
Watch, I've been waiting
for a captive audience.

76
00:04:20,760 --> 00:04:21,590
Huh?

77
00:04:22,260 --> 00:04:23,090
Hola!

78
00:04:23,440 --> 00:04:24,840
Buenas noches, General.

79
00:04:25,360 --> 00:04:28,160
I am José the Magnificent,
at your service.

80
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,140
Does he expect money?

81
00:04:52,680 --> 00:04:53,837
Oh, I get it.

82
00:04:53,920 --> 00:04:54,750
Let's get out of here.

83
00:04:54,833 --> 00:04:55,663
Right.

84
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:07,177
I read somewhere that there's an
ancient king buried in these ruins.

85
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:08,977
All right, maybe we'll see his ghost.

86
00:05:09,060 --> 00:05:10,354
Wouldn't that be cool?

87
00:05:15,040 --> 00:05:15,870
Calm down.

88
00:05:15,953 --> 00:05:16,899
He's just kidding.

89
00:05:17,920 --> 00:05:19,740
Okay, that is a little spooky.

90
00:05:21,880 --> 00:05:23,237
I'm not afraid of ghosts.

91
00:05:23,320 --> 00:05:24,150
I just tripped.

92
00:05:24,233 --> 00:05:25,137
Yeah, because it's dark.

93
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:26,050
That's it.

94
00:05:26,133 --> 00:05:28,214
It's dark, and you could get hurt, Ken.

95
00:05:29,240 --> 00:05:31,660
Sometimes I'm so smart it scares me. Huh?

96
00:05:32,500 --> 00:05:36,559
Sometimes you scare me, too, but I
think it's for a different reason.

97
00:05:36,820 --> 00:05:37,650
Gobble, Mon.

98
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:38,563
Sorry.

99
00:05:40,700 --> 00:05:44,137
He may be a goofy little glow worm,
but that light was a great idea.

100
00:05:44,220 --> 00:05:46,220
Geniuses are always misunderstood.

101
00:05:49,940 --> 00:05:51,897
Agatsuman, what's he doing here all alone?

102
00:05:51,980 --> 00:05:52,857
It doesn't matter.

103
00:05:52,940 --> 00:05:53,770
Come on, little guy.

104
00:05:53,853 --> 00:05:55,437
It's time to take you
back to the digital world.

105
00:05:55,520 --> 00:05:56,350
No!

106
00:05:57,240 --> 00:05:58,840
Hola, buenas noches.

107
00:05:59,300 --> 00:06:01,060
Hi, I mean, buenas noches.

108
00:06:01,480 --> 00:06:02,520
My name is Rosa.

109
00:06:02,880 --> 00:06:03,877
You're really cute.

110
00:06:03,960 --> 00:06:06,457
Now I'm double glad I sneaked
out of the house to help you.

111
00:06:06,540 --> 00:06:07,420
Who is she?

112
00:06:07,640 --> 00:06:10,097
She must be one of the
Mexican Digidestined.

113
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:14,197
She seems kind of young to be one of us,
but then again, she seems pretty brave.

114
00:06:14,280 --> 00:06:17,340
So, this crazy little guy
is your Digimon partner?

115
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:18,680
And who are you?

116
00:06:19,020 --> 00:06:23,961
Oh, my name is Ken, and these are my friends,
Matt, Gabumon, and my partner, Wormon.

117
00:06:26,840 --> 00:06:28,417
What did she say?

118
00:06:28,500 --> 00:06:29,440
I'm so scared.

119
00:06:29,660 --> 00:06:30,897
Would you hold my hand?

120
00:06:30,980 --> 00:06:32,697
What does she think she's doing?

121
00:06:32,780 --> 00:06:35,637
I don't know what she said, but
it's pretty clear what she's doing.

122
00:06:35,720 --> 00:06:36,550
Ken, Ken.

123
00:06:39,680 --> 00:06:41,900
You're a rude little girl. I'm what?

124
00:06:43,080 --> 00:06:44,040
Calm down, guys.

125
00:06:44,200 --> 00:06:46,177
There's no need for an
international incident here.

126
00:06:46,260 --> 00:06:47,697
There's enough of Ken to go around.

127
00:06:47,780 --> 00:06:49,977
Let's not forget why we're here, okay?

128
00:06:50,060 --> 00:06:50,897
Yeah, you're right.

129
00:06:50,980 --> 00:06:51,917
I know what I'm doing.

130
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:53,620
Ken, are you ready? Uh-huh.

131
00:06:54,420 --> 00:06:55,250
Sorry.

132
00:06:55,440 --> 00:06:56,320
Gusano! What?

133
00:06:57,440 --> 00:06:58,270
Come on, guys.

134
00:06:58,353 --> 00:06:59,183
No time to waste.

135
00:07:01,700 --> 00:07:03,935
Hey, Ken, what did Rosa just call him?

136
00:07:04,660 --> 00:07:05,490
Fishby.

137
00:07:05,573 --> 00:07:08,046
I don't think I'd tell
him that if I were you.

138
00:07:08,360 --> 00:07:09,260
It's not fair.

139
00:07:09,480 --> 00:07:12,774
She could at least insult me
in a language I understand.

140
00:07:14,240 --> 00:07:15,828
You're a warning next time?

141
00:07:16,220 --> 00:07:18,037
Silence, is this your idea of sneaking?

142
00:07:18,120 --> 00:07:19,137
They're right this way.

143
00:07:19,220 --> 00:07:20,338
Right, we're on it.

144
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:25,300
She's just young.

145
00:07:25,580 --> 00:07:27,357
So Ken, do you have a girlfriend?

146
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,557
If you don't, maybe you can move here.

147
00:07:29,640 --> 00:07:31,077
Then I could be your girlfriend.

148
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:32,337
Don't you think I'm cute?

149
00:07:32,420 --> 00:07:33,949
Who does she think she is?

150
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,937
I don't think that is what matters.

151
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,497
What matters is what she wants to be.

152
00:07:37,580 --> 00:07:39,240
Just call her Rosa Ichijoji.

153
00:07:39,580 --> 00:07:42,657
Wormon would rather bite off his
own tongue than call her that.

154
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:43,877
What's that up ahead?

155
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:46,313
I don't know, but I'll bet it's trouble.

156
00:07:50,400 --> 00:07:52,282
It's Minotauramon and Dokugumon.

157
00:07:52,380 --> 00:07:54,497
You're right, and they're
not at all happy to see us.

158
00:07:54,580 --> 00:07:56,857
Matt, these ruins are a
valuable historical site.

159
00:07:56,940 --> 00:07:57,857
We can't fight in here.

160
00:07:57,940 --> 00:07:58,770
We'll destroy them.

161
00:07:58,853 --> 00:07:59,683
He's right.

162
00:07:59,766 --> 00:08:01,457
We need a way to get them outside.

163
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:02,370
Outside, huh?

164
00:08:02,453 --> 00:08:03,283
We can do that.

165
00:08:03,366 --> 00:08:04,196
Be careful, huh?

166
00:08:04,279 --> 00:08:05,315
Gabumon, let's do it.

167
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:10,079
Is that a ring in your nose
or an allergic reaction?

168
00:08:13,620 --> 00:08:15,326
They are pretty good at this.

169
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:16,250
They practice.

170
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:28,760
It's all right, Rosa.

171
00:08:29,280 --> 00:08:30,456
Here, I'll kill you.

172
00:08:31,880 --> 00:08:33,300
We'll see about that.

173
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:35,970
Okay.

174
00:08:41,580 --> 00:08:42,410
No.

175
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,100
Darkseid, wait!

176
00:08:53,800 --> 00:08:55,360
Stop him. Where am I?

177
00:08:56,200 --> 00:08:57,030
Digimon.

178
00:08:58,680 --> 00:08:59,510
Digimon.

179
00:08:59,620 --> 00:09:01,540
Digimon, Digital Monsters.

180
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:02,995
We are the champions.

181
00:09:03,780 --> 00:09:05,720
Digimon, Digital Monsters.

182
00:09:05,900 --> 00:09:07,135
We are the champions.

183
00:09:12,060 --> 00:09:14,200
Nigi-Ball is your champion.

184
00:09:16,120 --> 00:09:17,860
Where's my Nigi-Ball too?

185
00:09:24,400 --> 00:09:25,230
Stingmon!

186
00:09:28,640 --> 00:09:32,097
Stingmon, these ruins are the last
will and testament of the Mayans.

187
00:09:32,180 --> 00:09:33,657
Try to leave them in one piece.

188
00:09:33,740 --> 00:09:35,564
Of course, I'm not a barbarian.

189
00:09:41,080 --> 00:09:41,910
Perfect.

190
00:09:41,993 --> 00:09:43,622
I never should have doubted you.

191
00:09:47,980 --> 00:09:50,509
And I thought you had
a hard hit, Gotsumon.

192
00:09:50,800 --> 00:09:51,780
This is dumb.

193
00:09:52,020 --> 00:09:53,897
They don't even seem to
care that we're here.

194
00:09:53,980 --> 00:09:55,317
I can bring them to their senses.

195
00:09:55,400 --> 00:09:57,640
Let's use Azulonmon's power. Right.

196
00:09:57,920 --> 00:09:59,017
Howl away, my friend.

197
00:09:59,100 --> 00:09:59,930
Yeah.

198
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,580
Digimon!

199
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:25,840
Koromon!

200
00:11:07,289 --> 00:11:08,119
NIGIGIGIMAN!

201
00:11:14,593 --> 00:11:15,423
Digimon, Digimon monsters,
Digimon are the champions!

202
00:11:15,506 --> 00:11:16,336
Gatsuma, Digimon, too!

203
00:11:16,419 --> 00:11:17,249
Monochromon!

204
00:11:19,980 --> 00:11:20,810
Monochromon!

205
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:25,580
I've had just about enough of you!

206
00:11:31,380 --> 00:11:32,740
Now is our chance, Ken.

207
00:11:33,040 --> 00:11:35,060
Send them back. My pleasure.

208
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:36,400
Digiport, open.

209
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:42,170
Ken?

210
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:44,280
Night-night. Huh?

211
00:11:46,760 --> 00:11:48,340
Stingmon, it's my home.

212
00:11:49,300 --> 00:11:51,712
Even when she's asleep, she's mean to me.

213
00:11:51,940 --> 00:11:52,840
Not at all.

214
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:55,457
She just said, Stingmon,
you're the greatest.

215
00:11:55,540 --> 00:11:56,370
Huh?

216
00:11:58,180 --> 00:11:59,768
Poor girl, she's exhausted.

217
00:11:59,880 --> 00:12:01,397
We'd better get her home to her parents.

218
00:12:01,480 --> 00:12:02,310
Delirious.

219
00:12:04,660 --> 00:12:06,080
Rosa, ¿eres tú?

220
00:12:06,740 --> 00:12:07,570
Mama?

221
00:12:07,653 --> 00:12:09,877
Rosa, don't you have any
idea how worried we've been?

222
00:12:09,960 --> 00:12:12,037
We were just about to call the police.

223
00:12:12,120 --> 00:12:14,637
Whatever were you thinking,
just wandering off like that?

224
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:15,550
That's no good.

225
00:12:15,633 --> 00:12:17,120
Oh, my goodness, you're all right.

226
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:21,740
Hey, Ken, how do you say
thank you in Spanish? Gracias.

227
00:12:22,560 --> 00:12:23,800
Gracias, Rosa.

228
00:12:45,040 --> 00:12:48,200
Let's finish this I'm hungry Yeah, me too

229
00:12:51,000 --> 00:12:52,300
Wine blade

230
00:12:57,500 --> 00:12:58,330
Rancorn!

231
00:13:23,560 --> 00:13:25,160
Okay, so where do we start?

232
00:13:25,960 --> 00:13:26,790
Anna.

233
00:13:27,040 --> 00:13:28,040
Hi, Anna.

234
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:31,270
Sonia.

235
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:32,620
Hi, Sonia.

236
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,490
Yuri.

237
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:36,880
Hey, Yuri.

238
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:40,420
That went well. Now what?

239
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,397
We're pleased to meet you.

240
00:13:42,480 --> 00:13:44,297
I'm Yoli, this is Sora, and these two...

241
00:13:44,380 --> 00:13:45,320
I'm Bielman.

242
00:13:45,540 --> 00:13:46,380
I'm Hawkbug.

243
00:13:51,100 --> 00:13:52,060
You're Anna.

244
00:13:52,840 --> 00:13:54,140
And Sonia, Yuri.

245
00:13:56,580 --> 00:13:57,760
Yoli, Sora.

246
00:13:58,480 --> 00:14:00,100
Bi-O-Mann and Hoch-Mann.

247
00:14:02,420 --> 00:14:04,500
Kirana and Sonia, Yuri.

248
00:14:06,160 --> 00:14:07,220
Yoli, Sora.

249
00:14:07,480 --> 00:14:08,720
Bi-O-Mann, Hoch-Mann.

250
00:14:10,380 --> 00:14:11,420
This is hopeless.

251
00:14:11,540 --> 00:14:13,357
Why didn't the others have this problem?

252
00:14:13,440 --> 00:14:15,300
We're just lucky, I guess.

253
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:18,937
Even if we can't understand each other's
words, we're all still Digidestined.

254
00:14:19,020 --> 00:14:19,850
Right.

255
00:14:19,933 --> 00:14:20,763
Let's try it again.

256
00:14:25,300 --> 00:14:26,535
This is embarrassing.

257
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:27,510
I'm not going to tell Tar.

258
00:14:27,593 --> 00:14:29,357
Where's Genie's friend or whatever he is?

259
00:14:29,440 --> 00:14:30,270
This is all bliss.

260
00:14:30,353 --> 00:14:31,200
This is disaster.

261
00:14:31,300 --> 00:14:33,497
The one with the purple
hair is kind of cute.

262
00:14:33,580 --> 00:14:35,520
Rightio, on to plan B.

263
00:14:37,240 --> 00:14:38,940
But I don't have a plan B.

264
00:14:39,220 --> 00:14:41,937
You'd better come up with one
unless you can read their minds.

265
00:14:42,020 --> 00:14:43,557
That'll happen when pigs fly.

266
00:14:43,640 --> 00:14:45,820
That's it. It is? We'll fly.

267
00:14:46,160 --> 00:14:47,180
See the Flymon?

268
00:14:47,860 --> 00:14:49,920
All of our Digimon can fly too.

269
00:14:50,780 --> 00:14:52,077
You know, fly.

270
00:14:52,160 --> 00:14:53,020
Fly, see?

